<title>UK: UK completes sale of MoD married quarters estate.</title>
<headline>UK completes sale of MoD married quarters estate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's the Ministry of Defence said on Tuesday it completed the sale of its Married Quarters Estate in England and Wales for 1.662 billion stg to Annington Homes, majority-owned by Nomura International.</p>
<p>Contracts for the controversial sale, which was criticised by Opposition politicians and veterans groups, were exchanged on September 24.</p>
<p>The Estate comprises some 57,400 homes, of which 2,400 are empty.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
</text>
